## So What?

The most consequential change today is that the site no longer claims the equation was "derived" anywhere — all five instances of that overclaim are now accurate. This removes the single most exploitable contradiction between the front page and the honest internal pages.

TEST-03 is the most interesting research finding: the framework may have crossed its own kill threshold and is currently in an unstated ambiguous state. The research proposal forces the archive to answer whether this is a failure, a mis-specification, or an ambiguity. Either outcome improves the framework's epistemic state.

The wide-binary slope remains the single highest-leverage missing piece. A quantitative slope prediction would make TEST-02 immediately testable against existing Gaia DR3 data. The explorer should prioritize this above any other physics topic.
